      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to 4}{log}_{2}⁡(4x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "The function ${log}_{2}⁡(4x)$ is well defined for $x>0,$ and so to find this limit we substitute $x=4$ into the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}{log}_{2}⁡(4x) & ={log}_{2}⁡(4\\cdot 4) \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(16) \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡({2}^{4}) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
